TUIOS (Terminal UI OS) is a terminal window manager and multiplexer in
the spirit of tmux and screen. It offers a vim-style modal interface,
tiling panes, nine workspaces and daemon-backed sessions that survive
detaching and restarts.

It can also serve sessions over SSH, with each connection getting its
own isolated instance, and the companion tuios-web program provides a
browser-based terminal. An inbox tracks the state of coding agents
running inside its panes.
